  "slug": "genetic-effects-1a8b",
  "summary": "AlphaGenome 2, lineage-resolved ChromBPNet scoring and the IGVF Catalog knowledge graph push variant interpretation toward cell-type and state resolution.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is resolving regulatory variant effects by cellular context. AlphaGenome 2 predicts cell-type-specific regulatory activity and variant effects from 1-Mb sequence across cell states. ChromBPNet models of 17 hematopoietic cell types score 302,830 variants and reveal lineage-structured accessibility effects. The IGVF Catalog integrates 657 variant-effect, regulatory-element and expression datasets into a queryable knowledge graph with API and LLM-agent access. Ancestry adds another axis: in admixed individuals, West African ancestry associates with more allele-specific expression, with 52 replicating loci. Disease-facing frameworks apply context to GWAS loci. EPIC2 links summary statistics to single-cell accessibility, and CAS-X and CELL-X prioritize type 2 diabetes effector genes via multi-tissue eQTLs and islet single-cell data. The endometriosis study cautions that cell-state prioritization depends on marker direction and donor structure. PrediXSKAT, which weights rare coding variants by predicted cis-regulated expression, and CATEomics, a toolkit for treatment-effect estimation, are more peripheral.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
